No high-confidence vulnerabilities found in b14ada40..HEAD.

The fixes close the Tera path: Tera's only opening delimiters are {{, {% and {# (the trim forms contain them). materialize.md step 3 checks the answer before escaping; the value is then written as a TOML basic string with \ and " escaped, so mise reads back exactly the answer; an escape cannot rebuild a delimiter. Nothing else setup writes is template-rendered — the only fill target is the conf.d fragment's marked positions.

Dropped candidates:
- _scripts/xcode delimiter check runs after mise has rendered the fragment (detection, not prevention); anyone who can commit the fragment can commit task code. 3/10.
- detect stdout holding a delimiter: refused; detect comes from trusted pack.yaml. 2/10.
- both-quote-kinds refusal is hardening, not a gap. 1/10.
